Pool PoolView; Running []RunningJob; Pause []PauseView; Ticks []TickView; Limits LimitsView; Issues []IssueView; Spend SpendView; Events []Event }`. `PoolView` carries Used and Max, plus `Waiting []Waiting{Role, Class, Reason (\"slot\"|\"limited\"|\"budget\"), Count, Oldest}`. `RunningJob` carries Issue, PR, Stage, Role, Model, Elapsed, Timeout and `FinishedCostUSD` (a `*float64`).\n   - `Sources` interface set: `PoolSource{Stats(); HeldSlots()}`, `LimitSource{Readings(); Until(family)}`, `StateSource{RunningJobs; JobUsage; IssueUsage; EndedSince or a new open-job listing; SpendSince}`, `ControlSource{PauseStates(); Ticks()}`, `Config func() *config.Resolved`, `Now func() time.Time`.\n   - `Taker.Take(ctx) Snapshot`: reads in-memory sources first, then SQLite through `state` only. The running-job cost comes from `JobUsage` (finished steps only, since `step_usage` rows are written when a step ends; the running step contributes nothing). Model and timeout come from the role config. `Limits` holds `Readings()` (utilization normalised to 0..1 via a new helper that handles both 0..1 and 0..100 streams, status, ResetsAt, age = Now − ObservedAt) and `Until(FamilyOf(model))` for opus, sonnet, haiku and \"\". Issues are the open `ard:` state plus jobs since 00:00 UTC, with the total from `IssueUsage` summed and cached per issue, invalidated by a new `Taker.Invalidate(issue)` / a generation bumped from close-out (cache key: issue + latest job `UpdatedAt`, to avoid touching closeout code). Spend is today's `SpendSince` against `cfg.BudgetUSDPerDay` and the role caps (reuse `budget.Gate.Capped`/`TokenReport` rather than new logic).\n   - Take must never use `github.*`: the package must not import `internal/github` (an import test enforces this).\n   - `events.go`: `Ring` (fixed size, mutex, `Append`, `Events()` copy) and `NewTee(next slog.Handler, ring *Ring) slog.Handler`, a handler that forwards to `next` unchanged and records time, level, message and a flattened attr string (use `redact` on the text; honour `WithAttrs` and `WithGroup`). Output of `next` must stay byte-identical.\n5. `internal/servecmd/serve.go` (wiring only): wrap the serve logger with the tee and construct a `snapshot.Taker` from the pool, limits book, store, budget gate and controller, keeping it available for the `ard serve` UI of #414. It is not rendered yet, so `ard serve` output does not change. A tee on the logger passes everything through to the existing handler.\n6. `docs/layout.md`: add `internal/snapshot/` line (and the new pool/controller accessors if layout lists them). Run `make docs-check` if it covers layout.\n\n### Test plan\nCommand: `make lint test` (`go test ./...`, plus `go vet`, `gofmt -l`).\n- `internal/pool/pool_test.go`:\n  - `TestRefusalsLimited` and `TestRefusalsBudget`: Offer candidates with the `Limited` or `Budget` hook set; `Stats().RefusedBy` shows role, reason and count, `WaitingBy` is unchanged and decisions equal the earlier verdicts.\n  - `TestRefusalsDoNotReserve`: with a refused candidate present, a second loop's grants are identical to a run with the hooks unset for that candidate (the grant decisions are unchanged).\n  - Refusals expire after the TTL; `TestHeldSlots` lists adopted and granted slots.\n- `internal/controller`: `TestPauseStatesRecorded` (the label pause appears per claiming loop, a non-claiming loop shows none, and a fake `Pauser` counts exactly one `Check` per tick, none from `PauseStates()`), `TestTicksRecorded`.\n- `internal/snapshot/snapshot_test.go` (table tests with fakes): pool used/max; waiting reasons `slot`, `limited`, `budget` per role; a running job whose finished steps cost 0.40 plus a running step reports 0.40 (cost of finished steps only), and one with no steps reports nil; elapsed against timeout; every active kill switch (config, label, pause-file, status-unreadable); tick times; readings (normalised utilization, status, resetsAt, age) and a block from `Until`; issues (open `ard:` state; job since 00:00 UTC; a job at 23:59 yesterday excluded) with a total cost and the cache (a second Take makes no second `IssueUsage` call, and Invalidate forces one); spend against the daily caps, and a nil config.\n- `TestTakeMakesNoGitHubCall`: use the GitHub fake (`internal/github` fake) wired to the pause gate and status reader; take 3 snapshots and assert zero recorded requests. Plus an import test that `internal/snapshot` has no dependency on `internal/github`.\n- `internal/snapshot/events_test.go`: ring overflow keeps the newest N in order, concurrent Append is race-free (`go test -race`), and the tee forwards a record byte-identically to a plain handler with attrs and groups.\n- Failure cases: a state read error leaves other fields filled and records the error in `Snapshot.Errors`; a nil config; empty book.\n\n### Risk\nMedium. The pool change is small but sits in the grant path; it must only add counters after the existing verdict is set (the dedicated unchanged-grant test covers it). The pool takes `p.mu` for the new reads, so keep them short (concurrency). The controller gains new shared state under `c.mu`. The slog tee wraps the logger for all of serve, so a bug would affect all log output (the byte-identical test covers it); redact text before storing. No migration, no public CLI change, and no protected paths (`.github/`, `.ard/config.yaml`, scanners, triage) are touched.\n\n### Size\nL (roughly 900 to 1,300 changed lines including tests, within the block limit). Files: `internal/pool/{pool,stats,slot}.go` and `pool_test.go`; `internal/controller/{controller,scheduler}.go` and a test; new `internal/snapshot/{snapshot,events}.go` with their tests; `internal/servecmd/serve.go`; `docs/layout.md`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ac2717e-3db0-4b55-ad8d-06af62537ab9","uuid":"33feb09d-7bf8-46c7-81fd-8fae46510da6","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:47:41.351Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"costs\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nwork